[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186164433 :answer-field/choices 17592186164434] [:db/retract 17592186164433 :answer-field/choices 17592186164435] [:db/retract 17592186164433 :answer-field/choices 17592186164436] {:db/id 17592186167229 :question/problem "![](images/9a/9aa8e2fec9812145eba6ef3add63dfcf16c9ddeb5557c3d37ef511947ace2e52.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i},$ where $a,b\\in R,$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that the given curve is $\\text{bounded}$ (and closed), representing $\\text{an ellipse}$ (circle) that is traversed $\\text{clockwise}.$\n\nBut we have that:\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a>0,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a<0.$\n\nThus, we must have $a=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164443 :answer-field/correct 17592186164445 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164440 :answer-field/correct 17592186164441 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164437 :answer-field/correct 17592186164439 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164433 :answer-field/correct "answer-5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" "answer-e0d1f152-2d71-5a47-a7da-fd041217b7f8" "answer-d93ff637-1a41-5c2a-a409-3b1e7bff5ef7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer/id #uuid "5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0d1f152-2d71-5a47-a7da-fd041217b7f8" :answer/id #uuid "e0d1f152-2d71-5a47-a7da-fd041217b7f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d93ff637-1a41-5c2a-a409-3b1e7bff5ef7" :answer/id #uuid "d93ff637-1a41-5c2a-a409-3b1e7bff5ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186385185 :question/problem "![](images/95/95ad67abf7291e83476f26216aac2b48a91adf3da102ca73ffab2a29c9716514.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-5}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\nHence, \n{{field-6}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d990f3a7-db2b-51f0-8db9-f30c83207610" :activity/id #uuid "d990f3a7-db2b-51f0-8db9-f30c83207610" :activity/title "Phase 